Answer: Variables can be declared by explicitly specifying their data types.

```java
int a = 10;
double b = 3.147;
char c = 'X';
String d = "Rama";
boolean e = true;
```

Answer: Type inference is the process of determining the type of a variable from the value assigned to it. Example:

```java
var a = 10;
var b = 3.147;
var c = 'X';
var d = "Rama";
var e = true;
```

Answer: The + operator can be used to combine text with a variable value. Example:

```java
var a = 10;
var b = 3.147;
var c = 'X';
var d = "Rama";
var e = true;
System.out.println("Data in A is " + a);
System.out.println("Data in B is " + b);
System.out.println("Data in C is " + c);
System.out.println("Data in D is " + d);
System.out.println("Data in E is " + e);
```

Output: Data in A is 10 Data in B is 3.147 Data in C is X Data in D is Rama Data in E is true

